<EnglishInstitutionalPage
  title="Cookie Policy | Canapalandia"
  description="Canapalandia Cookie Policy covering technical tools, optional analytics, consent duration and how to change your choice."
  canonical="/en/cookies/"
  alternateIt="/cookie-policy/"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  heading="Cookie Policy"
  lead="By default, Canapalandia uses only what is needed for the site to function. Optional measurement tools are activated only after your consent."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Cookies and similar tools</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small pieces of data that a website can store in the browser. Other technologies also exist, such as localStorage, technical identifiers and measurement scripts. On this page, the term “tools” includes both categories.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Necessary tools</h2>
    <p>Some information is stored locally because it is needed to remember choices made by the user and is not used for advertising profiling.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Theme preference:</strong> remembers light or dark mode.</li>
      <li><strong>Privacy choice:</strong> remembers whether you accepted or rejected the analytics category.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Optional analytics</h2>
    <p>Only after positive consent may the site activate the measurement category, which includes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics 4:</strong> statistical analysis of site use;</li>
      <li><strong>Ahrefs Analytics:</strong> traffic and content-performance analysis;</li>
      <li><strong>Vercel Web Analytics:</strong> site-usage statistics;</li>
      <li><strong>Vercel Speed Insights:</strong> measurement of real-world performance and Core Web Vitals.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you choose “Reject” or close the panel, these optional tools are not loaded by Canapalandia's configuration. Browsing and content remain available.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How your choice is stored</h2>
    <p>The preference is saved in the browser through a local record containing the consent-mechanism version, the analytics choice and the date. The system asks again after approximately six months or when the consent mechanism changes version.</p>
    <p>If you clear browser data, use private browsing or change device, you may be asked to make the choice again.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to change your mind</h2>
    <p>You can reopen the panel at any time through <strong>Privacy preferences</strong> in the footer. If you withdraw previously granted consent, the page is reloaded to stop subsequent loading of optional tools; Google Analytics cookies for the domain are also removed when they can be technically identified.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>External resources and services</h2>
    <p>Some pages may load technical resources from external services, for example fonts, icons, CDNs or JavaScript libraries. These requests are separate from the analytics category described above and may involve ordinary network requests to the provider needed to display or execute the resource.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Additional information</h2>
    <p>For information on categories of processed data, providers and user rights, see the <a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. For specific requests, email <a href="mailto:info@canapalandia.com">info@canapalandia.com</a> or use the <a href="/en/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
    <p class="institutional-note">Last substantial update: 11 August 2026.</p>
  </section>
</EnglishInstitutionalPage>
